 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137. I checked this by running the suite, not with separate tests for each rule.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test that `None` counts as not flagged in `monitor_flag_rate` (it also checks that an empty list gives `0.0`). I also added a test that `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last of several records with the same id.\n- **Item 11:** The README entry for `flags_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries, not `days + 1`. `daily_flag_counts` has a new entry.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest against SPEC turned up these fixes:\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now skips empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` returns `None` for empty groups and orders its keys by group name.\n  - `longest_alert_streak` now resets its run count when it hits a day with no flags.\n  - I reworded its docstring and README line from \"server alerts\" to \"consecutive days with flags\".\n  - I also changed the README line for `dedupe_transcripts` to say it keeps the last duplicate.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_transcript_log` raise a `ValueError` naming the line number for those. If you'd rather it handle them differently, that is a one-line change.",
